Subject: local: run the behaviour suite against an external mint

NOT FOR UPSTREAM as written. The behaviour suite selects its install driver
from ENVIRONMENT, which accepts only dev and stage, both of which deploy a
Cloudflare mint for the pool. RepoPoolExternalMint, which uses a mint that is
already running at FULLSEND_MINT_URL, exists but cannot be selected.

ENVIRONMENT=external now selects it, with these choices:

- the pool is laid out like stage: the single unsuffixed halfsend org, with
  BEHAVIOUR_POOL_SIZE slots;
- each slot is installed vendored by default, as the dev (pull request)
  path installs the build under test, or non-vendored at
  BEHAVIOUR_FULLSEND_REF when that is set, as the stage path installs main;
- setup names BEHAVIOUR_APP_SET when it is set, so it asks for the Apps the
  mint was configured with. Unset, the CLI default is kept, as before.

Together with 0017 and GITHUB_API_URL, this runs the suite against
Breadboard's GitHub emulator and Fullsend Mint. Gap BT-H3 of
.ledger/plans/fullsend-behaviour-tests-plan.md; BT-H4 (pool org names) needs
no change, because Breadboard seeds an emulator org named halfsend.

Breadboard note: test-only, like 0017; applied by the behaviour-test run, not
by deploy/scripts/05i-build-fullsend.sh.

diff --git a/pkg/behaviourtest/drivers/env/env.go b/pkg/behaviourtest/drivers/env/env.go
index c6357cca5..88da0721c 100644
--- a/pkg/behaviourtest/drivers/env/env.go
+++ b/pkg/behaviourtest/drivers/env/env.go
@@ -65,8 +65,8 @@ func (c RunnerConfig) Validate() error {
 	if c.CI != "githubactions" {
 		return fmt.Errorf("unsupported BEHAVIOUR_CI %q", c.CI)
 	}
-	if c.Environment != "dev" && c.Environment != "stage" {
-		return fmt.Errorf("unsupported ENVIRONMENT %q (want dev or stage)", c.Environment)
+	if c.Environment != "dev" && c.Environment != "stage" && c.Environment != "external" {
+		return fmt.Errorf("unsupported ENVIRONMENT %q (want dev, stage or external)", c.Environment)
 	}
 	return nil
 }
